statement:
Let $ABC$ be a triangle in which no angle is $90^\circ$. For any point $P$ in the plane of the triangle, let $A_1$, $B_1$, $C_1$ denote the reflections of $P$ in the sides $BC$, $CA$, $AB$ respectively. Prove that
\begin{enumerate}
\item[(i)] If $P$ is the incenter or an excentre of $ABC$, then $P$ is the circumcenter of $A_1B_1C_1$;
\item[(ii)] If $P$ is the circumcenter of $ABC$, then $P$ is the orthocenter of $A_1B_1C_1$;
\item[(iii)] If $P$ is the orthocenter of $ABC$, then $P$ is either the incenter or an excentre of $A_1B_1C_1$.
\end{enumerate}
